WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.731
A checklist for every server you ship or install.

2
00:00:03.011 --> 00:00:20.696
For servers you write: every input validated beyond its schema, with adversarial tests; read and write in separate tools, writes idempotent and gated by a human in the host; outputs small, cleaned, and labeled as data; no stdout writes on stdio; no token passthrough,

3
00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:31.280
audience checked, minimal scopes on HTTP; and a pinned tools/list snapshot in CI, so you notice your own definition changes before your users do.

4
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:48.157
For servers you install: remote if possible; publisher, exact name, and pinned version checked; every description read; isolated with its own narrow credentials, a single directory, and no unneeded network; write tools on ask; and an inventory you revisit.

5
00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:51.339
The lab gave you a server that follows the first list.

6
00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:57.293
The second list is a habit, and the next time you add a server to Claude Code is the time to start it.
